turning this robot on  is all that hong yi lu needs to do  before it turns its attention to him  the researcher at sweden's royal  institute of technology has designed a  breakthrough in how people and robots  work together  his robot can recognize and even predict  his gestures and wishes  such as pass me that spanner instead of  slowing down or stopping if a human gets  too close  basically i want a robot to work with me  similar as a human co-worker  to hand me over the right tool at right  time at right location  which is not happening right now in the  industry so i wanted to  break the barrier between human robot  the barrier is reduced by a scanner that  works out each person's body structure  to prevent any collision between metal  and flesh  a robot that can predict a human's  actions and adapt to them can be a game  changer in this  field but sweden's success with this  kind of technology  is also down to how humans have adapted  to robots  swedish heavy industry already makes  wide use of robotics  workers fears of being replaced are  eased at least in theory by a generous  welfare state  and strong trades unions that insist on  retraining when a machine takes over  this office in malmo may not look like a  hive of robotic activity but behind the  scenes  or rather in the cloud robot reporters  are doing the work of thousands of  journalists  turning data on sports matches real  estate weather and traffic  accidents into written reports it would  be fair to say that we have  maybe caused a couple of of journalists  jobs to to disappear  but that is only because they were doing  stuff that machines can do better  we do the simple repetitive reporting  they can do the more qualitative  high-level  reporting the robotic scoops are ready  for the morning edition of the barometer  newspaper in calmer and at dozens of  national and local titles across sweden  the robot is actually one of our most  contributing  reporters it's all about having more  content  to offer to our readers back at the lab  in stockholm  the goal is for robot human relations to  be about collaboration not competition  if we can introduce a robot to help a  human operator  together they form a new team they can  be more productive  in the industrial setting robots may now  be able to avoid  harming a human's body but it might take  a very hard-headed employee  to stop worrying about robots harming  their job prospects  paul reese al jazeera stockholm
 

